  "what_this_is": "Whether each of the 23 issuers has entity-wide XBRL facts for shares outstanding and for public float in the SEC's company-concept API, and when they were filed. Counts, forms and filing dates only: no value was kept. It says what could be had point-in-time from the SEC; nothing was added to the dataset.",
  "method": {
    "provider": "SEC EDGAR XBRL company-concept API, https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyconcept/CIK##########/dei/<concept>.json",
    "concepts": [
      "EntityCommonStockSharesOutstanding",
      "EntityPublicFloat"
    ],
    "how": "A same-origin fetch loop run in a data.sec.gov tab of the built-in browser, because data.sec.gov supports no cross-origin scripting; one request per issuer and concept, 300 ms apart (about 3 a second; the SEC's stated maximum is 10 a second). A page script cannot set a user agent, so the browser sent its own.",
    "requests_for_this_result": 46,
    "requests_in_all": "about 110: an aborted first loop (15 requests, stopped by a TypeError on HURN's empty unit entry before anything was kept), one request to inspect that entry, one for ACHV, a shape-only loop (46) and the loop that produced this result (46)",
    "retrieved_at": "2026-10-09T05:13:53.660Z",
    "window": [
      "2024-10-01",
      "2026-10-02"
    ],
    "first_event_day": "2024-11-04",
    "kept": "per issuer and concept: the status, the unit, the number of facts, the forms, the first and last filing date, the facts and distinct filing dates inside the window, and whether a fact was filed by 2024-11-04",
    "not_kept": "every fact's value, period end, accession number and fiscal period",
    "transcription": "The page computed the SHA-256 of its canonical output; the text was saved to a file and its length and SHA-256 were recomputed in Python and matched."
  },
