  "limits": [
    "Entity-wide facts only: the company-concept API does not aggregate dimensional facts, so an issuer that reports shares by class (OKTA, and JBSS since 2012) shows no usable fact here although its filings state the shares.",
    "A filing date is the date of the original filing in the API's fact list; amendments appear as further facts with later dates, and the check did not look at values or at which fact supersedes which.",
    "Public float is the aggregate market value of non-affiliate common equity on one date a year (the last business day of the second fiscal quarter), reported in the annual report: it is not a share count and not free float.",
    "Shares outstanding come from the cover page as of a date near the filing; they are not updated between filings.",
    "The SEC says the XBRL APIs update in under a minute and filings appear on sec.gov a few minutes after acceptance, and does not guarantee either; a filing's availability time is therefore its filing date plus a margin, not a measured instant."
